# Accepted image-scan findings, read by Trivy from the repository root.
#
# Each entry is a decision, not a silence: it names the finding, why it is
# accepted, how that was verified, and the date it lapses. Past its `exp:` date
# an entry stops applying and the `images` check fails again — on purpose. Never
# add an entry without one, and never widen it beyond the IDs named.
#
# CVE-2026-75804, CVE-2026-84782 — OpenSSL, libssl3t64 3.5.7-1~deb13u2 in the
# distroless nodejs26-debian13 base. Debian fixed both in 3.5.7-1~deb13u3;
# distroless had not republished on 2026-10-01, and the newest `:nonroot`
# digest still ships deb13u2, so no Dockerfile change can move it.
# Accepted because nothing in either image loads that library. The node binary
# links no system libssl (it carries its own OpenSSL), and of every ELF file in
# the published prisme-api and prisme-web images — the argon2 and sharp addons
# and libvips included — only OpenSSL's own libraries and engines link libssl
# or libcrypto.
# Remove both entries in the pull request that moves the base image to a digest
# shipping deb13u3. Recorded in docs/50-journal/P0-2026-10-01-dependabot-wave.md.
CVE-2026-75804 exp:2026-10-15
CVE-2026-84782 exp:2026-10-15
